+# v39 — parameter power/log repair and endpoint-strategy record
+
+## Current run evidence
+
+The v38 results passed 15/19 gates: the accepted 14-gate baseline and the new
+fixed-coefficient statement interface. One window-parameter build failed; three
+parameter descendants were blocked. The 147 distinct passing theorem audits use
+only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. The seven newly accepted interface
+results are not a candidate-count bound at any positive coefficient.
+
+## Source changes
+
+Only the pending `Endpoint/WindowParameters.lean` and `Endpoint/CutoffParameters.lean`
+mathematical modules change. No existing theorem statement, hypothesis, parameter
+definition or numerical constant changes.
+
+The reported rewrite expected power notation while the target used `Real.rpow`.
+Mathlib already supplies `Real.rpow_eq_pow`, whose proof is reflexivity. The shared
+`log_div_rpow_eq` adapter normalizes that representation and proves
+
+    log(u / Real.rpow v r) = log u - r * log v,  u != 0, v > 0.
+
+The window logarithmic-difference proof and corresponding cutoff proof now use
+that single adapter. Two other pending cutoff sites explicitly normalize real
+power notation before the existing logarithm and power-addition rules. These
+cutoff changes are proactive; the uploaded run did not reach those declarations.
+
+The adapter gets an expanded exact-type example and transitive axiom target.
+All existing audit targets and examples are retained. There are still 19 gates;
+the branch theorem inventory grows from 42 to 43. The runner changes only its
+unique results prefix to `erdos647_repo_v39_results_`.
+
+## Endpoint strategy
+
+Preserve the exponent a=log 2/(1+log 2), the scale (log X)^a/log(log X), all current
+internal parameters and t=1/(1000 log(log X)). The output coefficient is any
+explicit fixed c>0 justified by the complete argument. No replacement constant
+is made mandatory; the provisional 1/2000 candidate is removed from the status
+record. The statement interface is accepted but `proved_coefficient` remains null.
+
+Work order:
+
+1. Exact parameter asymptotics.
+2. An eventual fixed positive gap lambda-B_H >= delta H.
+3. Every amplified error term, including the factorial tail and CRT remainder.
+4. Final assembly with a comfortable explicit fixed c>0.
+
+Derive the old EndpointClaim only if the resulting proved coefficient is at least
+1/1000 at essentially no extra effort. Do not optimize an arbitrary coefficient
+or weaken the exponent/scale. The accepted finite, PNT, Mertens, factorial and
+debit proofs are not reopened.
+
+## Preservation and PR scope
+
+All 41 currently accepted mathematical modules are unchanged (the accepted
+40-module baseline plus the statement interface), as are the two other pending
+parameter modules. Lean/Mathlib 4.32.2, lockfiles, upstream source, warning policy,
+axiom allowlist, CI files, core API and existing build/cache directories stay
+unchanged. The old fixes PR remains complete; the new parameter PR still awaits
+its four limit gates. No remote write or PR operation is included.
